    "metadata": {
      "title": "Integration Assessment: Sequencing the Path to EUR 8.2m Synergy",
      "author": "Integration Management Office",
      "company": "Steering Committee",
      "date": "7 September 2026"
    }
  },
  "children": [
    {
      "name": "section",
      "children": [
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "cover",
            "slots": {
              "title": "Integration Assessment: Sequencing the Path to EUR 8.2m Synergy",
              "subtitle": "Post-Acquisition Steering Committee Briefing",
              "client": "Steering Committee",
              "date": "7 September 2026",
              "confidentiality": "Confidential — Steering Committee Only"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "section",
      "children": [
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "running-head",
            "slots": {
              "confidentiality": "Confidential — Committee Only",
              "date": "7 September 2026"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "section-opener",
            "slots": {
              "number": "01",
              "title": "Customer and Depot Overlap Create a Clear Path to €8.2m Synergy",
              "tracker": "Baseline"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "key-takeaways",
            "slots": {
              "items": [
                "Customer overlap of 31% and depot overlap of 12 of 41 sites enable rapid consolidation.",
                "€8.2m of annual synergy is available, but 40% depends on a dispatch system neither firm has budgeted.",
                "Fund the dispatch migration in month one to protect the full synergy run-rate."
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "kpi-row",
            "slots": {
              "items": [
                {
                  "value": "31%",
                  "label": "Customer accounts overlapping"
                },
                {
                  "value": "12/41",
                  "label": "Depots with direct overlap"
                },
                {
                  "value": "€8.2m",
                  "label": "Annual synergy identified"
                }
              ],
              "source": "Integration due diligence, Sept 2026"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "text": "Overlap analysis confirms that 31% of the combined customer base is served by both companies today, and 12 of the enlarged group's 41 depots sit within the same catchments, creating direct scope for site and route consolidation. Of the identified €8.2m in annual synergy, 60% — largely procurement, corporate overhead and depot rationalisation — is available within eighteen months using existing systems. The remaining 40%, worth roughly €3.3m a year, depends on migrating both companies onto a single dispatch system, a project neither company has costed or budgeted, and which therefore becomes the critical path for the second half of the case."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "section",
      "children": [
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "section-opener",
            "slots": {
              "number": "02",
              "title": "A Phased Sequence Captures Most Synergy Before the System Migrates",
              "tracker": "Sequence"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "text": "The recommended sequence front-loads no-regret actions that need no system change: consolidating overlapping depots' back-office functions, harmonising procurement contracts and integrating corporate overhead in the first six months. Depot-level route and dispatch consolidation in the 12 overlapping sites follows once a dispatch system decision is funded, targeted for month seven. By month eighteen this sequence realises the full 60% first tranche of synergy — about €4.9m annually — without depending on the system migration's completion."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "chart-figure",
            "slots": {
              "chart": {
                "name": "highcharts",
                "props": {
                  "width": "100%",
                  "options": {
                    "chart": {
                      "type": "column",
                      "width": 900,
                      "height": 460
                    },
                    "title": {
                      "text": null
                    },
                    "xAxis": {
                      "categories": [
                        "Months 1–6",
                        "Months 7–12",
                        "Months 13–18"
                      ]
                    },
                    "yAxis": {
                      "title": {
                        "text": "Cumulative synergy (€m)"
                      }
                    },
                    "series": [
                      {
                        "name": "Recommended sequence",
                        "data": [
                          1.6,
                          3.4,
                          4.9
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              },
              "caption": "Cumulative synergy captured reaches €4.9m by month 18 under the recommended sequence",
              "takeaway": "The full first-tranche synergy of €4.9m is achievable without waiting on the dispatch system, provided migration funding is secured in month one.",
              "source": "Integration Management Office synergy model, Sept 2026"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "text": "This first tranche depends only on organisational and contractual integration, not on the dispatch system migrating successfully. The month-one funding decision therefore sits outside this trajectory: it does not change what is achievable by month eighteen, but it determines whether the remaining 40% of the case starts moving at all."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "section",
      "children": [
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "section-opener",
            "slots": {
              "number": "03",
              "title": "Six-Month Milestones Anchor Depot Consolidation to System Funding",
              "tracker": "Milestones"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "text": "Each six-month milestone pairs a depot-consolidation target with a dispatch-system decision, so the steering committee can track whether the funding gap is closing. The first milestone requires only a capital-allocation decision, not a working system, and is the gating action for everything that follows."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "data-table",
            "slots": {
              "title": "Six-Month Milestones: Depots, Synergy and System Migration",
              "labelHeader": "Milestone",
              "labels": [
                "Depots consolidated (of 12 overlap)",
                "Synergy captured, cumulative (€m)",
                "Dispatch migration, % complete"
              ],
              "columns": [
                {
                  "header": "Month 6",
                  "cells": [
                    "3.0",
                    "1.6",
                    "20.0"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "header": "Month 12",
                  "cells": [
                    "7.0",
                    "3.4",
                    "45.0"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "header": "Month 18",
                  "cells": [
                    "9.0",
                    "4.9",
                    "70.0"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "source": "Integration Management Office milestone plan, Sept 2026"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "callout",
            "slots": {
              "label": "Funding gate",
              "text": "Neither company has budgeted the dispatch migration. The month-one milestone assumes steering committee approval of a dedicated capital line for system selection and implementation, separate from integration operating costs."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "section",
      "children": [
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "section-opener",
            "slots": {
              "number": "04",
              "title": "Deferring the Migration a Year Forfeits About €3.3m and Raises Execution Risk",
              "tracker": "Risk"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "text": "Deferring the dispatch migration by a year pushes the entire system-dependent tranche — 40% of the case, about €3.3m annually — out of the eighteen-month window entirely, since that tranche cannot be realised until the migration is complete and stabilised. The delay also stalls depot consolidation in the 12 overlapping sites, because closing a depot requires routing its work through a shared dispatch system first, so those sites continue running two systems and two cost bases for an extra year. The 31% of customers served by both companies are the most exposed during that period, experiencing inconsistent service levels and booking processes for longer, which raises retention risk precisely where competitors are most likely to target the newly combined business. Securing the migration budget at the month-one milestone is therefore the single decision that protects the largest component of the synergy case."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "block",
          "props": {
            "ref": "footnotes"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
